<title>USA: Time Warner to sell American Lawyer Media.</title>
<headline>Time Warner to sell American Lawyer Media.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Time Warner Inc said Friday it had signed a definitive agreement to sell American Lawyer Media L.P. to Cranberry Partners, an entity managed by investment bank Wasserstein Perella.</p>
<p>Terms of the deal were not disclosed.</p>
<p>American Lawyer Media, based in New York, publishes a number of national and regional trade newspapers and magazines serving primarily the legal community.</p>
<p>Time Warner said the transaction is expected to close by the end of August, subject to regulatory and other conditions.</p>
</text>
